1
00:00:04,779 --> 00:00:08,679
Chapter 21.

2
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:18,119
It was then that the fox appeared.

3
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:30,698
"Good morning," said the Good morning," the little prince responded politely,

4
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:36,179
although when he turned around he saw nothing

5
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:44,198
I'm right here," the voice said, "under the apple tree."

6
00:00:44,198 --> 00:00:53,520
"Who are you that's the little prince, and added, "You are very pretty to look at."

7
00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:03,039
"I am a fox the fox said Come and play with me propose the little prince.

8
00:01:03,039 --> 00:01:06,460
"I am so unhappy."

9
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:14,500
"I cannot play with you," the fox said I'm not tamed."

10
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,359
"Ah!

11
00:01:16,359 --> 00:01:26,039
Please excuse me," said the little prince with some confusion But, after some thought, he added:

12
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:30,719
"What does that mean-- 'tame'?"

13
00:01:30,819 --> 00:01:35,800
"You do not live here," said the fox.

14
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,658
"What is it that you are looking for?"

15
00:01:39,698 --> 00:01:43,779
"I am looking for men," said the little prince.

16
00:01:43,779 --> 00:01:47,800
"What does that mean-- 'tame'?"

17
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:52,000
"Men," said the fox.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,760
"They have guns, and they hunt that is very disturbing.

19
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:00,639
They also raised chickens.

20
00:02:00,639 --> 00:02:04,179
These are their only interests.

21
00:02:04,179 --> 00:02:07,960
Are you looking for chickens?"

22
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:13,300
"No," said the little prince I'm looking for friends.

23
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:17,618
What does that mean-- 'tame'?"

24
00:02:17,618 --> 00:02:23,139
"It doesn't act too often neglected," said the fox.

25
00:02:23,139 --> 00:02:28,319
It means to establish ties."

26
00:02:28,779 --> 00:02:32,198
"'To establish ties'?"

27
00:02:32,198 --> 00:02:37,079
"Just that," said the fox.

28
00:02:37,539 --> 00:02:41,560
"To me, you are still nothing more than a little boy who is just like a hundred

29
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,539
thousand other little boys.

30
00:02:43,539 --> 00:02:46,000
And I have no need of you.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,600
And you, on your part, have no need of me.

32
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:54,698
To you, I am nothing more than a fox like a hundred thousand other foxes.

33
00:02:54,698 --> 00:02:58,719
But if you tame me, then we shall need each other.

34
00:02:58,719 --> 00:03:02,560
To me you'll be unique in all the world.

35
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:08,939
To you, I shall be unique in all the world..."

36
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:14,198
"I am beginning to understand," said the little prince.

37
00:03:14,198 --> 00:03:17,279
"There is a flower...

38
00:03:17,859 --> 00:03:22,439
I think that she has tamed me..."

39
00:03:22,479 --> 00:03:26,920
"It is possible," said the fox.

40
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:31,300
"On the Earth one sees all sorts of things."

41
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:34,840
"Oh, but this is not on the Earth!"

42
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:37,060
said the little prince.

43
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:42,340
The fox seemed perplexed, and very curious.

44
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:44,560
"On another planet?"

45
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,420
"Yes."

46
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:49,118
"Are there hunters on that planet?"

47
00:03:49,118 --> 00:03:57,819
"No that is interesting now they're chickens?"

48
00:03:57,819 --> 00:04:00,779
"No."

49
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:13,840
"Nothing is perfect side the folks But he came back to his idea.

50
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:18,939
"My life is very monotonous he said.

51
00:04:18,939 --> 00:04:22,719
"I hunt chickens; men hunt me.

52
00:04:22,719 --> 00:04:27,579
All the chickens are just alike, and all men are just alike.

53
00:04:27,579 --> 00:04:32,079
And, in consequence I'm a little bored.

54
00:04:32,079 --> 00:04:38,859
But if you tame me, it will be as if the sun came to shine on my life.

55
00:04:38,859 --> 00:04:43,179
I shall know the sound of a step that will be different from all the others.

56
00:04:43,179 --> 00:04:47,920
Other steps send me hurrying back underneath the ground. Yours will call me,

57
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:51,399
like music, out of my burrow.

58
00:04:51,399 --> 00:04:55,479
And then look: you see the grain Fields down yonder?

59
00:04:55,479 --> 00:04:58,238
I do not eat bread. Wheat is of no use to

60
00:04:58,238 --> 00:05:01,899
me. The wheat fields have nothing to say to me.

61
00:05:01,899 --> 00:05:04,060
And that is sad.

62
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:07,479
But you have hair that is the color of gold.

63
00:05:07,479 --> 00:05:11,319
Think how wonderful that will be when you have tamed me!

64
00:05:11,319 --> 00:05:17,979
The grain, which is also golden, will bring me back the thought of you.

65
00:05:17,979 --> 00:05:23,219
And I shall love to listen to the wind in the wheat..."

66
00:05:23,439 --> 00:05:28,679
The fox gaze the little prince, for a long time.

67
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:32,738
"Please-- tame me!"

68
00:05:32,738 --> 00:05:35,020
he said.

69
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:40,300
"I want to, very much," the little prince replied.

70
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:49,060
"But I have not much time. I have friends to discover, and a great many things to understand."

71
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:55,359
"One only understands the things that one tames," said the fox.

72
00:05:55,359 --> 00:05:59,139
"Men have no more time to understand anything.

73
00:05:59,139 --> 00:06:02,500
They buy things already made at the shops.

74
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:11,380
But there is no shop anywhere where one can buy friendship, and so men have no friends anymore

75
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:16,179
If you want a friend, tame me..."

76
00:06:16,179 --> 00:06:22,420
"What must I do, to tame you ask the little prince.

77
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:27,880
"You must be very patient," replied the fox.

78
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:36,100
"First you will sit down at a little distance from me-- like that-- in the grass.

79
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:43,139
I shall look at you out of the corner of my eye, and you will say nothing.

80
00:06:43,139 --> 00:06:47,979
Words are the source of misunderstandings.

81
00:06:47,979 --> 00:06:54,060
But you will sit a little closer to me, every day..."

82
00:06:55,238 --> 00:07:00,719
The next day the little prince came back.

83
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:06,100
"It would have been better to come back at the same hour," said the fox.

84
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:11,859
"If, for example, you came at four o'clock in the afternoon, then at three o'clock I

85
00:07:11,859 --> 00:07:17,380
shall begin to be happy. I shall feel happier and happier as the hour advances.

86
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:22,840
At four o'clock, I shall already be worrying and jumping about. I shall show

87
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,939
you how happy I am!

88
00:07:24,939 --> 00:07:31,000
But if you choose to commit just any time, I shall never know at what hour my heart

89
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,819
is to be ready to greet you...

90
00:07:33,819 --> 00:07:44,198
One must observe the proper rights What is a right That's the little prince.

91
00:07:44,198 --> 00:07:52,198
"Those also are actions too often neglected," said to the fox

92
00:07:53,859 --> 00:08:02,260
the rights I want to make one day different from other days continued the fox

93
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:05,920
one hour from other hours.

94
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:09,579
There is a right for example, among my hunters.

95
00:08:09,579 --> 00:08:16,719
Every Thursday they dance with the village girls. So Thursday is a wonderful day for me!

96
00:08:16,719 --> 00:08:20,979
I can take a walk as far as the vineyards.

97
00:08:20,979 --> 00:08:27,219
But if the hunters danced at just any time one day would be like every other day,

98
00:08:27,219 --> 00:08:32,579
and I should never have any vacation at all."

99
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:36,219
So the little prince tamed the fox.

100
00:08:36,219 --> 00:08:40,800
And when the hour of his departure drew near

101
00:08:43,118 --> 00:08:48,399
said the fox, "I shall cry."

102
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:52,539
"It is your own fault," said the little prince.

103
00:08:52,539 --> 00:08:58,779
"I never wished you any sort of harm; but you wanted me to tame you..."

104
00:08:58,779 --> 00:09:04,539
"Yes, that is so," said the fox.

105
00:09:04,539 --> 00:09:10,238
"But now you are going to cry little prince.

106
00:09:10,238 --> 00:09:16,840
"Yes, that is so," said the fox.

107
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:20,920
"Then it is don't you no good at all!"

108
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:30,939
"It has done me good," said the fox, "because of the color of the wheat fields."

109
00:09:30,939 --> 00:09:37,600
And then he added: "Go and look again at the roses.

110
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:43,139
You will understand now that yours is unique in all the world.

111
00:09:43,658 --> 00:09:52,439
Then come back to say goodbye to me, and I will make you a present of a secret."

112
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:05,399
The little prince went away, to look again at the roses.

113
00:10:06,158 --> 00:10:10,719
"You are not at all like my rose," he said.

114
00:10:10,719 --> 00:10:13,060
"As yet you are nothing.

115
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:18,460
No one has tamed you, and you have tamed no one.

116
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:20,679
You are like my fox when I first saw him.

117
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:25,238
He was only a fox like a hundred thousand other foxes.

118
00:10:25,238 --> 00:10:32,439
But I have made him my friend, and now to me he's unique in all the world

119
00:10:32,439 --> 00:10:36,819
than the roses were very much embarrassed.

120
00:10:36,819 --> 00:10:42,039
"You are beautiful, but you are empty you went on.

121
00:10:42,039 --> 00:10:44,618
"One could not die for you.

122
00:10:44,618 --> 00:10:48,719
To be sure, an ordinary passerby would think that my rose looked just like you--

123
00:10:48,719 --> 00:10:51,639
the rose that belongs to me.

124
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:55,300
But in herself alone she is more important than all the hundreds of you

125
00:10:55,300 --> 00:11:02,319
other roses: because it is she that I have watered visited she that I have put under the

126
00:11:02,319 --> 00:11:06,819
glass globe; because it is she that I have sheltered behind the screen; because

127
00:11:06,819 --> 00:11:11,079
it is for her that I have killed the caterpillars (except the two or three

128
00:11:11,079 --> 00:11:16,359
that we save to become butterflies); because it is she that I have listened

129
00:11:16,359 --> 00:11:23,460
to, when she grumbled, or boasted, or even sometimes when she said nothing.

130
00:11:23,738 --> 00:11:29,399
Because she is my rose.

131
00:11:30,219 --> 00:11:34,439
And he went back to meet the fox.

132
00:11:35,979 --> 00:11:40,300
"Goodbye," he said.

133
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:44,760
"Goodbye," said the fox.

134
00:11:45,399 --> 00:11:52,139
"And now here is my secret, a very simple secret:

135
00:11:53,020 --> 00:12:01,359
It is only with the heart that one can see rightly; what is essential

136
00:12:01,359 --> 00:12:05,520
is invisible to the eye."

137
00:12:05,618 --> 00:12:13,060
"What is essential is invisible to the eye," the little prince repeated,

138
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:17,039
so that he would be sure to remember.

139
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:27,520
"It is the time you have wasted for your rose that makes your rose so important."

140
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:35,139
"It is the time I have spared and spent for my rose--" said the little prince,

141
00:12:35,139 --> 00:12:39,600
so that he would be sure to remember.

142
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:46,539
"Men have forgotten this truth," said the fox.

143
00:12:46,539 --> 00:12:49,420
"But you must not forget it.

144
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:55,118
You become responsible, forever, for what you have tamed.

145
00:12:55,118 --> 00:12:59,760
You are responsible for your rose..."

146
00:13:00,939 --> 00:13:09,238
"I am responsible for my rose," the little prince repeated,

147
00:13:09,639 --> 00:13:15,840
so that he would be sure to remember

148
00:13:16,539 --> 00:13:19,260
foreign
